# OSS-Phone-V1 stage-2 containment liveness marker.
#
# Appended to init.rc by magiskinit and run by the CONTAINED Android init
# (inside its PID + mount namespace). It writes one marker to the global kernel
# log as soon as the container reaches second stage. oss-init (the real PID 1)
# reads /dev/kmsg -- which is global and visible across namespaces, and needs no
# mount -- and takes the marker to mean "the container is past first-stage
# SwitchRoot and watchdogd is starting", so its early-hang breaker stands down.
#
# This deliberately adds NO mount: v2's shared /oss-run tmpfs broke Android's
# SwitchRoot (which moves every mount under / into the read-only system root)
# and caused the boot loop. A kernel-log write is mount-free and cannot affect
# SwitchRoot.
#
# The marker string must match LIVENESS_MARKER in oss-init.c exactly.

on early-init
    write /dev/kmsg OSSPHONE_CONTAIN_LIVE

on init
    write /dev/kmsg OSSPHONE_CONTAIN_LIVE
